.TH KALO 1 "November 2026" "Kalo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kalo \- send and receive files over Bluetooth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kalo
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kalo
is a small Bluetooth file-sharing application. With no subcommand it opens
the graphical window. Files are sent and received with the Object Push
Profile (OPP) through BlueZ and obexd; incoming files are saved to the user's
Downloads directory.
.PP
The receiver registers an OBEX agent on the session bus. Only one agent can
own that slot at a time (for example, Blueman's transfer service may hold it).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ui
Open the graphical application (the default).
.TP
.B adapters
List Bluetooth adapters and their state.
.TP
.B connectable \fR[\fIon\fR|\fIoff\fR]
Show or change the adapter's connectable state.
.TP
.B devices \fR[\fB\-\-discovery\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
List devices known to BlueZ, optionally after a discovery window.
.TP
.B pair \fIMAC\fR
Pair with a device by address.
.TP
.B agent\-check
Check whether the OBEX agent slot is free and release it again.
.TP
.B send \fIMAC\fR \fIFILE\fR
Send a file to a device over OPP.
.TP
.B receive
Run the receiver in the foreground. Incoming pushes are accepted; this is the
command-line equivalent of leaving the UI open.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME ,
.B HOME
Locate obexd's staging directory. Received files are moved to the XDG
Downloads directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR obexctl (1),
.BR obexd (1)
.SH BUGS
Incoming pushes are currently accepted from every device; the trust store is
not implemented yet.
